Chapter: RocAliasEmpty
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ported from roc-lang/roc, src/eval/test/eval_closure_recursion_tests.zig,
 "inspect: list alias empty list aliasing", case 14 in file order:

     { x = [] y = x match y { [] => 42, _ => 0 } }

 and Roc expects 42.

 An EMPTY list bound, then aliased, then read through the alias. It is the
 aliasing cluster's version of the shape finding 58 is about: an empty literal
 has no element to answer from, and here nothing downstream constrains it
 either -- the only thing ever asked of it is its length. So the element type
 is genuinely unconstrained, which makes this a case where refusing would be
 honest and answering is better.

 Adaptations, standing: `list-length` for the pattern, and `42.0` is `42`.

Section: Functions

  alias-empty : Integer -> Integer
  alias-empty (n) =
   let x = []
   in let y = x
   in if list-length y == 0 then 42 else 0

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni (show (alias-empty 0))
  end
